由 \(\tan \alpha=\frac{3}{4}\)，可得：

\[
\cos^2\alpha=\frac{1}{1+\tan^2\alpha}
=\frac{1}{1+\left(\frac{3}{4}\right)^2}
=\frac{1}{1+\frac{9}{16}}
=\frac{16}{25}
\]

又因为：

\[
\sin 2\alpha=\frac{2\tan\alpha}{1+\tan^2\alpha}
=\frac{2\cdot \frac{3}{4}}{1+\frac{9}{16}}
=\frac{\frac{3}{2}}{\frac{25}{16}}
=\frac{24}{25}
\]

所以：

\[
\cos^2\alpha+2\sin 2\alpha
=\frac{16}{25}+2\cdot \frac{24}{25}
=\frac{16}{25}+\frac{48}{25}
=\frac{64}{25}
\]

